    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d341">

                <pb facs="0456" n="368" sameAs="frus:frus1904/pg368"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Brown to Mr. Hay.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >American Legation,<lb/>Guatemala and Honduras</hi>,<lb/><hi
                                rendition="#italic">Guatemala</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1904-05-23"><hi rendition="#italic">May 23,
                                1904</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 175.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Referring to instruction No. 97 of February
                    25 last, concerning the Renton claim against Honduras, I have the honor to
                    transmit herewith a copy with translation of the reply received to the
                    legation’s representations, stating that the Honduran Government desires a just
                    solution of the matter and expressing the hope that it will be possible for
                    Minister Combs to confer personally with the Honduran Government at Tegucigalpa
                    respecting this case.</p>
                <p>I have, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Philip Brown.</hi></signed></closer>


                <xi:include href="d341-a1.xml" xpointer="d341-a1"/>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
